# Overwrites the stock default.conf the nginx image ships in conf.d.
#
# conf.d cannot be a read-only mount any more — it is where the image writes
# the rendered roller.conf — so the stock file is no longer shadowed by our
# own. It declares `server_name localhost` on :80, and an exact name match
# beats our `default_server`, so requests with that Host reached nginx's
# welcome page instead of the site.
#
# Rendering an (almost) empty file over it is the least surprising fix: it uses
# the same envsubst step as the real config rather than adding a mount or an
# entrypoint hook.
